Lab 4: Block repeated attackers with fail2ban

sudo apt install -y fail2ban
sudo nano /etc/fail2ban/jail.local

[DEFAULT]
bantime = 1h
findtime = 10m
maxretry = 5
ignoreip = 127.0.0.1/8 192.168.10.0/24

[sshd]
enabled = true
port = ssh
backend = systemd

sudo systemctl restart fail2ban
sudo fail2ban-client status
sudo fail2ban-client status sshd

# remove a ban by mistake
sudo fail2ban-client set sshd unbanip 192.168.20.55

To test, fail SSH logins from a lab machine five times; its address appears in the banned list. This turns the "stop password guessing" requirement into automatic action.